# Cloudflare Workers Assets reads this file (it is never served itself).
#
# The client is a single unhashed index.html, so a cached copy is a *stale app*,
# not just stale markup — old timing logic, old tabs, old bugs. That has bitten
# twice: players kept hitting a draft-lock that had already been moved, because
# their browser was still running the previous deploy.
#
# no-cache does not mean "don't store"; it means "revalidate before use". The
# browser still keeps the file and still gets a 304 when nothing changed, so
# this costs one conditional request, not a full download.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# The service worker especially must never be sticky — a stale one keeps
# serving old push behaviour long after a deploy.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
